        <mxCell id="jfZI8W6IYFFo4_fwkGy_-37" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=13;spacing=8;" value="Part B: What normal form is this data in (before normalization)?&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;1NF.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Not 0NF: the data has a primary key (RespondentID + GenreID), no duplicate rows (every RespondentID-GenreID pair is unique), and no multivalued attributes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Not 2NF: it has partial dependencies. RespondentID alone determines Respondent, Age, Hours, StreamingID, StreamingService, MentalHealth, and MusicEffect. GenreID alone determines Genre. Both are dependencies on only part of the composite primary key.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;At 1NF: the data has a PK, no duplicate rows, no multivalued attributes, and every non-key attribute is functionally dependent on at least part of the PK -- but it still has the partial dependencies above, so it does not reach 2NF." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="480" width="520" x="1860" y="290" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
